        "evidence": "Six spaced em-dashes in one block. Two are true parentheticals ('the nuclear degeneracy locus - the curve in the (p,A)-plane where adjacent nuclei have equal energy - forms', 'The **degeneracy locus** - the set of (p,t) where ... - satisfies') and one is a legitimate double-question ('Whether ... - and whether ... - remains an open question'). Three are load-bearing: 'There is no approximation - the integer minimiser ...' dodges a colon; '... to multi-baryon nuclear structure - the same passage that takes the proton ... to a nucleus' appends an afterthought; and '... even-odd staggering is most pronounced - precisely where the degeneracy locus would intersect the stability curve' appends an unsupported claim to the end of a sentence, where it reads as established. Density is the tell.",
